'''DSA DEADLINE: EXEMPTION MOTION FAILS 241-232 — Tsubaki-ya Saved by Community Fund; 5,400 Donors Raise ¥2.3M in 12 Hours; "The Government Could Not Save Me. The People Did."'''
The DSA exemption motion — businesses with fewer than 20 employees — failed in the Diet today. 241-232. Nine votes short. The motion was not retroactive. Even if it had passed, Tsubaki-ya's deadline was today. But the Shintenchi-doro Merchants' Association launched a volunteer fund at 6:00 AM. By 6:00 PM, 5,400 donors had contributed ¥2.3M — an average of ¥426 per donor. Tsubaki-ya is saved. Not by the government. By the community. Tsubaki Mie, 68, owner of Tsubaki-ya for 31 years: "The government could not save me. The people did." Organiser Yamashita Kenji, 52, owner of the stationery shop next door: "Tsubaki-ya is the street. If it closes, the street loses its memory." The excess ¥500K will establish the permanent Shintenchi-doro Small Business Relief Fund for DSA compliance costs for businesses with fewer than 20 employees. The Mainichi notes: the government's DSA created the burden. The community created the solution. The market worked where the Diet did not.

'''FOREIGN MINISTRY: NINETY SECONDS — Junior Spokesperson Reads Statement; FM Does Not Appear; No Questions; Press Conference Announced for Tomorrow 9 July'''
The Foreign Ministry announced a press conference for 10:00 AM today. The press corps assembled. The Foreign Minister did not appear. Deputy Director Hayashi Yuki, 34, a junior spokesperson from the Public Affairs Division, stepped to the podium. She read a prepared statement. The statement lasted 90 seconds. She did not take questions. The statement: "The Foreign Ministry is aware of the MV Castellano situation. The Ministry has notified the relevant embassies. The Ministry has identified the shipping company as Marítima Estrella S.A. The Ministry has requested the Balboan government to provide Marítima Estrella's corporate records. The Ministry has initiated a review of Zong Trade Bridge Ltd.'s commercial activities in Okaiken. The Ministry will hold a full press conference on 9 July. The Foreign Minister will appear. Thank you." The Mainichi notes: the statement addressed the Castellano. The statement did not address the Ayorin attacks. The statement did not address the eleven days of silence. The FM will speak tomorrow.

'''MV CASTELLANO: FIRST MATE TESTIMONY — False Wall Built at Port of Balboa City; Crew Informed After Departure; "Couriers, Not Organisers"; 13 Crew Members Refuse to Cooperate'''
The first mate's testimony to the Justice Ministry has revealed new details about the false wall construction. The first mate testified that the false wall in Cargo Hold 3 was built at the Port of Balboa City by Marítima Estrella dockworkers — not by the crew. The crew was informed of the cargo after departure. The first mate: "We were told the container held machinery parts. After we left Balboa, the captain told me there was something else. I did not know what. I did not ask." The first mate is the only crew member cooperating. The remaining 13 crew members have refused to cooperate through their attorney, Kishi Daisuke: "Our clients maintain their right to silence." The Mainichi notes: the crew are couriers, not organisers. The wall was built in Balboa. The question is: who at Marítima Estrella ordered the construction? Who at Zong Trade Bridge knew?

'''ZONG AMBASSADOR RESPONDS — 36 Hours After Notification; "Conditional Cooperation"; "Zong Trade Bridge Is a Commercial Entity, Not a State Entity"'''
The Zong ambassador has responded to the drug notification — 36 hours after the Sansi ambassador. The Zong Embassy statement: "The Zong Federation is prepared to offer conditional cooperation. Zong Trade Bridge Ltd. is a commercial entity, not a state entity. The Zong government does not direct the commercial activities of private firms. We await the results of the Okaiken investigation before determining the scope of our cooperation." The Mainichi notes: the Sansi ambassador responded in 24 hours with unconditional cooperation. The Zong ambassador responded in 36 hours with conditions. The Balboan embassy has not responded. The conditions are being evaluated by the Foreign Ministry.

