| editorial =
'''EDITORIAL: The Market and the Street'''
The DSA exemption motion failed. 241-232. Nine votes. The government could not save Tsubaki-ya. The community did.

5,400 donors. ¥2.3M in 12 hours. An average of ¥426 per donor. The Shintenchi-doro Merchants' Association organised the fund in six hours. The fund was launched at 6:00 AM. By 6:00 PM, it had exceeded the ¥1.8M DSA compliance cost by ¥500K. The excess will establish a permanent relief fund for small businesses facing DSA compliance costs.

The Mainichi has been writing about Tsubaki-ya for weeks. The DSA was designed for large systems. The DSA was not designed for a cake shop with three employees. The Diet debated the exemption motion. The Diet voted. The motion failed by nine votes. Nine votes separated a small business from closure.

But the community did not wait for the Diet. The community did not wait for the government. The community organised. The community donated. The community saved Tsubaki-ya. And the community created a model — the Shintenchi-doro Small Business Relief Fund — that can be replicated across Okaiken.

The Mainichi notes: the government's DSA created the burden. The community created the solution. The market worked where the Diet did not. This is not a critique of the DSA — the DSA is necessary for digital sovereignty. This is a critique of the DSA's failure to distinguish between large systems and small businesses. The exemption motion failed. The community fund succeeded. Both are true. Both are Okaiken.

'''SHIRATORI KENJI — Ninety Seconds'''
Eleven days of silence. Ninety seconds of statement. The Foreign Ministry has spoken — but barely.

The FM did not appear. The FM sent a 34-year-old deputy director who has never handled a press conference. The statement lasted 90 seconds. No questions were taken. The statement addressed the Castellano. The statement did not address the Ayorin attacks. The statement did not address the eleven days of silence. The statement did not address the diplomatic cascade — Burawa, Asikyira, Hersatia.

The FM will hold a full press conference tomorrow. The FM will appear. The FM will take questions. The Mainichi will be there. The questions will not be 90 seconds.

The Mainichi notes: the first mate is talking. The Sansi ambassador is talking. The Zong ambassador is talking — conditionally. The community is talking. The press corps is talking. The Foreign Ministry is reading. There is a difference. The Foreign Ministry will learn it tomorrow.

